<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Flip Normals</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Mesh &gt; Normals &gt; Flip</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Flip Normals</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command inverts the normals of all selected and visible polygons. This means that if an object is convex, after the operation it will be concave, and vice versa. This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
